   "id": 518751,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Maggie invests $3,000 in an account that earns 5.1% interest compounded monthly. How much is the account worth after 13 years?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The future value of an investment, <span data-math=\"A\"></span>, when the principal, <span data-math=\"P\"></span>, is invested at an annual interest rate of <span data-math=\"r\"></span> (in decimal form), compounded <span data-math=\"n\"></span> times per year for <span data-math=\"t\"></span> years is found using the formula <span data-math=\"A = P{\\left({1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)^{nt}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><i>Hint</i>: Find <span data-math=\"nt\"></span> before you plug numbers into your calculator! <span data-math=\"nt = \\left({12} \\right)\\left({13} \\right) = 156\"></span> It will help you get the right results. Use those parentheses in your calculator, too!</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = 3,000{\\left({1 + \\frac{{0.051}}{{12}}} \\right)^{156}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A \\approx \\$ 5,813.64\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$5,813.64"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
